From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Conijn <egc112@msn.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 20:52:52 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: b43: HT-PHY: receive A-MPDUs of up to 64 KiB

Advertise a maximum A-MPDU length of 64 KiB on HT-PHY too, and raise
the ucode's limits for it as on N-PHY, as brcms_c_ampdu_shm_upd() does
for that factor: the watchdog (M_WATCHDOG_8TU) to 10 and the longest
PSDU (M_MIMO_MAXSYM) to 0xffff.

Upload from an ath11k client, the two versions alternated run by run
(30 s each): Netgear R6400 v2 (BCM4331) 92.2 and 88.8 Mbit/s with
32 KiB, 107 and 105 Mbit/s with 64 KiB (+17 %); R6400 v1 91.4 and
88.2 against 82.2 and 93.2 Mbit/s (no clear difference).

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Erik Conijn <egc112@msn.com>
[rosenp: reuse the N-PHY defines and code instead of adding them again]
Signed-off-by: Rosen Penev <rosenp@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/b43.h  | 2 +-
 drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c | 9 +++++----
 2 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/b43.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/b43.h
@@ -332,7 +332,7 @@ enum {
 #define  B43_SHM_SH_UCODESTAT_SUSP	3	/* suspended */
 #define  B43_SHM_SH_UCODESTAT_SLEEP	4	/* asleep (PS) */
 #define B43_SHM_SH_MAXBFRAMES		0x0080	/* Maximum number of frames in a burst */
-#define B43_SHM_SH_MIMO_MAXSYM		0x00BA	/* Longest PSDU received, N-PHY (bytes) */
+#define B43_SHM_SH_MIMO_MAXSYM		0x00BA	/* Longest PSDU received, N/HT-PHY (bytes) */
 #define B43_SHM_SH_WATCHDOG_8TU		0x003C	/* RX A-MPDU watchdog (8 TU); was DEFAULTIV */
 #define B43_SHM_SH_SPUWKUP		0x0094	/* pre-wakeup for synth PU in us */
 #define B43_SHM_SH_PRETBTT		0x0096	/* pre-TBTT in us */
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c
@@ -5863,10 +5863,11 @@ static int b43_wireless_core_init(struct
 	 * A timeout of zero is infinite. */
 	b43_shm_write16(dev, B43_SHM_SHARED, B43_SHM_SH_PRMAXTIME, 1);
 	/*
-	 * Receive A-MPDUs of up to 64 KiB on N-PHY, as brcmsmac does for
-	 * that factor: the longest PSDU to 64 KiB and its watchdog to 10.
+	 * Receive A-MPDUs of up to 64 KiB on N-PHY and HT-PHY, as brcmsmac
+	 * does for that factor: the longest PSDU to 64 KiB and its watchdog
+	 * to 10.
 	 */
-	if (dev->phy.type == B43_PHYTYPE_N) {
+	if (dev->phy.type == B43_PHYTYPE_N || dev->phy.type == B43_PHYTYPE_HT) {
 		b43_shm_write16(dev, B43_SHM_SHARED, B43_SHM_SH_MIMO_MAXSYM,
 				0xFFFF);
 		b43_shm_write16(dev, B43_SHM_SHARED, B43_SHM_SH_WATCHDOG_8TU,
@@ -6513,7 +6514,7 @@ static void b43_ht_cap_set_chains(struct
 	if (rx_ss >= 2)
 		ht_cap->mcs.rx_mask[1] = 0xff;
 	/* The firmware takes up to 64 KiB, see b43_wireless_core_init() */
-	if (dev->phy.type == B43_PHYTYPE_N)
+	if (dev->phy.type == B43_PHYTYPE_N || dev->phy.type == B43_PHYTYPE_HT)
 		ht_cap->ampdu_factor = IEEE80211_HT_MAX_AMPDU_64K;
 	if (tx < 2)
 		ht_cap->cap &= ~IEEE80211_HT_CAP_TX_STBC;
